# ── THE RAW GTFS FEED, 20 SEP 2026 ──────────────────────────────────
# Rejseplanen's open timetable is 331 MB unzipped. It landed in public/ first,
# which would have shipped a third of a gigabyte to Vercel on every deploy,
# because Vite copies that folder verbatim into dist/. Oliver moved it to the
# project root the same evening, which fixes the deploy and leaves the other
# half: it is still inside the repository and would still be committed.
#
# NO LEADING SLASH, so this matches a folder called GTFS at any depth. That
# covers where it was, where it is, and wherever the next copy is unzipped,
# which is the point: this is a working file that gets re-downloaded rather
# than a location anybody maintains.
#
# NOTHING READS IT AT RUNTIME AND NOTHING SHOULD. What the app needs was
# extracted into src/data/ferryRoutes.js, which is a few kilobytes and is
# committed. Re-download from rejseplanen.info/labs/GTFS.zip when that extract
# needs refreshing, which is about once a year for the question it answers.
GTFS/
